1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,824
Is your daily coffee really the reason you never have any money?

2
00:00:04,174 --> 00:00:08,230
Five dollars a day adds up to about eighteen hundred dollars a year.

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:15,767
Invest that instead for thirty years at around seven percent, and it could grow to about a hundred and eighty five thousand.

4
00:00:16,117 --> 00:00:19,480
Sounds huge. But here's what the coffee argument leaves out.

5
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:26,401
For most households, the biggest costs are housing, transport and food. That is where real savings hide.

6
00:00:26,751 --> 00:00:31,909
Paying three hundred less on rent saves twice as much as skipping every coffee all year.

7
00:00:32,259 --> 00:00:35,363
So enjoy the coffee. Just fix the big stuff first.
